W906-PASSPROF (tools/wb_serve.cpp): QPC phase timer on the existing WdMark points (28 marks on existing main-loop lines, 64 slots + '(more phases)'); a pass >= W906_SLOWPASS_MS (default 100, min 5) writes one op-log SLOW line: wall ms, tick-thread CPU ms (QueryThreadCycleTime / rdtsc) and the top 10 phases. Sub-phase marks through ht9045::g_W906PhaseMark (FastClockJobs.cpp; 0 in every ctest): heater beat, DoThermo, DoThermoReal case 100 steps and every COM2 StopComm / StartComm (bthermo.cpp), MotorAccessTick parts (WebMotorAccessLive.cpp). All marks sit on existing lines (no line moves) except wb_serve.cpp EOF.

What the profiler found (release, IO thread 30 ms, idle, no HMI, nothing pressed): the main thread WAITING (low CPU) inside DoThermoReal:
(1) COM2 StopComm 11-16 ms each, ~10-14 times per 90 s -- golden resets the port (case 2500 retries spent) when a DTK4848 address does not answer. Probe: writer join 0.1-2 ms, reader join up to one 15.6 ms Sleep(1) tick, CloseHandle(COM2) 11-12.7 ms (driver).
(2) HeaterSVLog in the first ~40 s after boot, once per channel: slHeaterLog is the 3-arg TMyStringList (MaxLineCount=1) so every second line is a synchronous open/append/close on D:\HT9045_Log (golden does the same). Left as is (boot / SV change only).

W906-COMM-STOPFAST (vclcompat/Comm.cpp, no line moves except EOF): the reader's idle Sleep(1) waits on a manual-reset stop event instead (same tick; StopComm sets it -> reader join 0.05-0.13 ms); StopComm hands the port handle to a short-lived closer thread; StartComm (before the exclusive re-open), the next StopComm and ~Impl wait for it (5 s cap). golden's reset sequence (StopComm, 0.5 s, StartComm) unchanged.

Also: W906-TEMPLOG-DIR (csystem.cpp) TemperatureStorageLog's MyForceDirectories cached per path, rechecked at most every 60 s; Pci1203ModuleCheck idle() -> W906_Pci1203ModuleCheckTick returns at once when nothing is pending.

Measured after: COM2 StopComm gone from the SLOW lines; after the boot window heater 20 ms beats missed 0-1 per 10 s (busy avg ~2.6 ms); ping p50 1.8 ms.

o2 full build 0 errors; ctest 381/399, failures = the known list (ThermoComm [5] and ScanKeyGolden [14] source pins were broken by same-line marks on the first run; the marks moved off those anchors, both pass); production_audit: every change was written at 13:24:34 by the measurement wb_serve's normal close, 0 files touched after 13:25 (ctest wrote nothing), baseline re-snapshotted; Debug then release wb_serve rebuilt. Machine question for EastSun: COM2 keeps being reset = some DTK4848 addresses never answer (Addr 1/2/4/5/8 seen). WORKLOG item 132.

